# CLI Usage Quick Reference

- Executable: `you-up-cli` ([main.swift](mdc:Sources/you-up-cli/main.swift))
- Common commands:
  - `swift run you-up-cli` — full check
  - `--verbose` — show interfaces, routers, DNS servers, domains, endpoints
  - `--internet-only` | `--gateway-only` | `--dns-only`
  - `--json` — machine-readable output
  - `--show-config` — print config path, create sample if missing
- JSON fields mirror `NetworkStatus`:
  - `gateway.internet.dns.status` (string), `reachable` (bool), and `timestamp`.
- Configuration locations:
  - `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/you-up/endpoints.json` or `$HOME/.config/you-up/endpoints.json`
  - Sample creation handled by the CLI via `ConfigurationLoader`.

